    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e452037f_4cd0b9b6",
        "filename": "board/cr50/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 528,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-25T19:12:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Initially every time we reset the tpm we would reboot cr50. We didn\u0027t want to do this during a usb spi update, because it would kill the update. After the update, we reset the EC and AP, so the tpm would get reset then. \n\nNow we don\u0027t do the cr50 reboot during the tpm reset, and I feel like the tpm_is_resetting check in reset_tpm is enough to handle any weird side effects of us pulsing sys_rst_l. I don\u0027t think there is a good reason for this check any more.",
      "revId": "35d2f10c00c2f92573ad23da62a8cde69623174a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a75dca76_e1fa18ad",
        "filename": "board/cr50/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 557,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-24T22:08:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we catch every edge? Have you determined how quickly we can react?",
      "revId": "35d2f10c00c2f92573ad23da62a8cde69623174a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
