        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-24T22:08:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why are we waking on this signal falling? Especially if it\u0027s not even monitored for certain platforms.",
      "revId": "35d2f10c00c2f92573ad23da62a8cde69623174a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f0235b9_b684e08a",
        "filename": "board/cr50/gpio.inc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 121,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-25T19:12:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In board.c we disable the wake-pin for x86 platforms. On arm we still want to reset the tpm every time sys_rst_l is asserted so we want to wake up on the falling edge.\n\nWe could enable the wake pin only on ARM platforms in board.c but I would really like it to be easy to tell what is a wake pin from gpio.inc",
      "revId": "35d2f10c00c2f92573ad23da62a8cde69623174a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b00cf5c_dd8ea132",
        "filename": "board/cr50/gpio.inc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 121,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-25T22:56:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But the opposite is true: It\u0027s not really a wake pin for those types of systems. Now it\u0027s just a head scratcher as to what is going on. We should be consistent on where wakes/interrupts are being enabled. And since that is runtime dependent we should move it to the code where it\u0027s handled in runtime.",
      "revId": "35d2f10c00c2f92573ad23da62a8cde69623174a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
